From a5bc261a22c148218f673fbbc05fde4241028614 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:42:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Give one dark-roof explanation everywhere and remove
 stale notes

- README, notebooks 00/03/05, aoi.yaml and the report source now say the
  same thing: the negative dark-roof coefficient has no confirmed cause
  (shadow, rooftop clutter or sparse trees in the 10 m dark class), and dark
  roofs cover only ~0.5% of an urban block. Notebook 05 no longer claims
  shadow was ruled out (its argument used 30 m pixels; classes are 10 m).
- Notebook 01 no longer says EnMAP is pending; notebook 02 and classify.py
  no longer call the classes interim or 'three'; notebook 03 says which
  measures use the regression and which use published values.
- Remove references to CLAUDE.md, which the repository no longer contains.
- enmap_scenes.txt: the April scene is before the June-August LST window.
- Unity: import analysis figures without power-of-two rescaling (they were
  stretched in the Analysis maps pop-up); rename SAT LINK to ARCHIVE CHECK
  and RESIDENTS COOLED to RESIDENTS IN TREATED BLOCKS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019LPfV4rvbkEpTMU3bHqkjU
